useReducer()
-------------------

- It is a one Hook in React
- It is used to handle complex data of the Component
- It has same purpose of useState [i.e. state - store, manage the data]

How to store and manage the data using useReducer() hook

1. import useReducer() hook
2. Call the useReducer() hook
    it also return an array and having two elements as useState.

    in useReducer one is state,dispatch [special predefine function]

    let [state, dispatch] = useReducer()

3. useReducer() hook takes two arguments and they are

    1. function (reducer)
    2. Initial Data

let [state, dispatch] = useReducer(reducerFn, initialData)

initialData is stored in state
if we want to update state then reducer Function is used to update.
if we want to call reducer function then we use dispatch

reducer is a user Defined function, which is used to update the state.

Reducer function takes one parameter and that parameter is object type

Reducer function stores a special object in its Parameter and i.e. action object

Reducer function whatever it returns that data will update in the state.

Inside the Reducer Function we have to implement logic to update the state.

dispatch is a pre-defined function
dispatch is used to call reducer function
dispatch will re-return the component
dispatch can take one argument that is action object

action object
action object is a special object in react
action object should have one mendatory Property and i.e. type and whose value should be some unique string across the application.

    {
        type: "<unique string>"
        data : ""
    }

Apart from type Property, we can add any number if properties inside the action object.

state
dispatch
reducer
action object


Counter App with useReducer() Hook

whenever you are not performing multiple different action then better to go with useState().

if you are going to perform multiple action / operation then we use useReduce().



Redux 



this is a separate library.
it is not a part of React.


1. Create a Redux store
2. Make Redux Store available to each and every component of React Application.
3. Any Component can store the data in the Redux Store.
4. Any Component can access the data from Redux Store.

usecase:
1. Redux Enhance the Performance of the Application

How to Implimant Redux in React Application?

1. Install Redux Library
    npm install redux

2. Create a Redux Store
    import
    use that function

3. Make Redux Store Available to each and every component of the Application

    react-redux is another Library which is used to integrate React with Redux

    npm install react-redux

Redux
--------

Redux is a JavaScript Library and Pattern

Purpose of Redux
-----------------
To manage the state(data) of the application.
Using redux we can share the data between the components irrespective of the relationship.



steps:

1. Create the components

2. Create a Redux store.
    1. install Redux Library (npm i redux)
    2. import legacy_createStore()
    3. call the above function

3. Make Redux Store available to all the components of the application

    1. install react-redux (npm i react-redux)
    2. import Provider Component react-redux Library
    3. Wrap/Render App Comp inside the Provider Component
    4. Pass store props to the Provider component and assign redux store a s a value to it.

4. Store the Data from Component into the Redux Store

    Component -----> Redux Store    (storing the data)
    Redux Store -----> Component (Consume the data)

    1. create a reducer function.
    2. register reducer function to redux store
    3. Create a action object and store the component data in the action object as a second property.
    4. Call the dispatch() from the component and pass action object as a first argument to it.
    5. Configure a middleware called redux-logger with redux store
        1. install redux logger (npm i redux-logger)
        2. import logger
        3. configure with the store
    6. Access the data from the Redux Store in the React Component
        useSelectore(()=>{})
        - this takes a callback functon


Note:- whenever we start react application, internally redux will call reducer() function, and whatever data reducer will return it will store by default inside redux store as a initial data

Note :- 
----------
    We can't directly store the data into redux store.
    we need a reducer function to store the data into the Redux-Store


actionCreator
|
|
actionCreator is a simple JS function which returns action object.

Note:
-------
 - We can create only one redux store for a application.
 - Whenever we refresh or reload application, redux data will be removed or it will lost.
 - we cannot store data in the redux permanently.
 - redux is used for data/state manegment for perticular session.







JSON SERVER

- It is used to creating our API and test them

1. install jsonserver package

	npm i jsonserver	// old (Now not in use)

	npm install json-server  // latest

2. create db.json file under the application root folder

3. add the required data

4. start the json server

	jsonserver --path path/io/	// (old)

	npx json-server --watch db.json	// (latest)

5. Access the data using following url

	Endpoints for my db :	http://localhost:3000/result


